# Sting has flash: Bot1 casts it in Bot2's end step. "When Sting enters, put a hone counter on Sting for each creature target
# opponent controls. Attach Sting to up to one target creature you control." Bot2 controls two Ornithoppers, so Sting gets two hone
# counters, and attached to Bot1's Ornithopter it makes it 2/2 (CR 122.1j). Bot2's Ornithopters are not creatures Bot1 controls,
# so the second target refuses them (CR 115.1).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Sting, Bilbo's Sword
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sting, Bilbo's Sword.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sting, Bilbo's Sword.Counters.Hone = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Sting, Bilbo's Sword.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Power = 0
